cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "judgepanel: estimating LLM-judge accuracy without gold labels"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-05"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohammadi-hadi/judgepanel"
url: "https://github.com/mohammadi-hadi/judgepanel"
authors:
  - given-names: "Hadi"
    family-names: "Mohammadi"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0860-9200"
    affiliation: "Utrecht University"
keywords:
  - "LLM-as-judge"
  - "Dawid-Skene"
  - "label aggregation"
  - "inter-rater agreement"
  - "evaluation"
  - "large language models"
abstract: >-
  Estimates each judge's confusion matrix, the class prevalence, and a
  posterior over every item's true label from a panel of imperfect judges
  labelling the same items, with no gold labels, via the Dawid-Skene model
  fitted by EM. Includes majority-vote baselines, Cohen's and Fleiss' kappa,
  bootstrap confidence intervals, and panel simulators. Validated on a real
  five-judge panel over 400 agent trajectories where the estimated judge
  accuracies can be checked against construction-time gold labels, including
  an honest account of the correlated-judge failure mode.
